3. Regular Expression Field Extraction (rex)

Your sample raw log format is:

user="admin" session_id="sess_88192"


Under SPL rex Query, put:

| rex field=_raw "user=\"(?<user>[^\"]+)\"\s+session_id=\"(?<session_id>[^\"]+)\""

Regex Syntax Explanation

Put:

(?<user>[^\"]+) creates a named field called user and captures all characters inside the user value until the next quotation mark.

\s+ matches one or more whitespace characters between the user and session fields.

(?<session_id>[^\"]+) creates a named field called session_id and captures the session identifier from the raw log record.

4. Transaction Grouping (transaction)

Under SPL Transaction Query, put:

| transaction session_id
| eval associated_user=mvindex(user,0)
| eval session_outcome=if(match(mvjoin(status,","),"500|504"),"Failed","Successful")
| table session_id associated_user eventcount duration session_outcome

